      </constraints>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Hedge of Spears" id="3741-ddd9-455b-4136" hidden="false">
          <description>The warriors in a hedge of spears inflict a -1 penalty to their enemies’ rolls to hit.
This can stack with a spearman’s support.

Medieval texts covering the Rus’ and Varangians’ battle tactics describe a “wall bristling with spears.”

A hedge of spears works in the same way as a shieldwall, except with spears.
A hedge of spears can be combined with a shieldwall. In this case, the two effects stack: the defence bonus from the shieldwall and the penalty to enemy rolls to hit.
Every figure in the wall must be equipped with a shield AND a spear.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Weather" id="df4a-679e-62be-2c34" hidden="false">
          <description>Rus’ and Varangians aren’t affected by the effects of snow.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Romphaia" id="6347-f989-4929-faf3" hidden="false">
          <description>Rus&apos; and Varangians don’t strike last with their Dane axes. They fight simultaneously with this weapon, even when they haven’t charged.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Two Hand Weapons" id="413b-9bfb-7f72-da9d" hidden="false">
          <description>The Rus’ can carry two hand weapons to get an additional attack. This also inflicts a -1 penalty to their defence rolls.


A figure carrying two hand weapons can’t carry a shield or a ranged weapon.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </forceEntry>
  </forceEntries>
